{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q6AXS0","uniProtkbId":"NCLX_RAT","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2006-01-10","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-06-10","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2004-09-13","entryVersion":125,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Rattus norvegicus","commonName":"Rat","taxonId":10116,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Glires","Rodentia","Myomorpha","Muroidea","Muridae","Murinae","Rattus"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Mitochondrial sodium/calcium exchanger protein"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"14625281"}],"value":"Na(+)/K(+)/Ca(2+)-exchange protein 6"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"15060069"}],"value":"Sodium/calcium exchanger protein, mitochondrial"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"14625281"}],"value":"Sodium/potassium/calcium exchanger 6"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"RGD","id":"1565818"}],"value":"Solute carrier family 24 member 6"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"RGD","id":"1565818"}],"value":"Solute carrier family 8 member B1"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"RGD","id":"1565818"}],"value":"Slc8b1"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"14625281"}],"value":"Nckx6"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"15060069"}],"value":"Nclx"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"RGD","id":"1565818"}],"value":"Slc24a6"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q925Q3"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"40931067"}],"value":"Mitochondrial sodium/calcium antiporter that mediates sodium-dependent calcium efflux from mitochondrion, by mediating the exchange of 3 sodium ions per 1 calcium ion (By similarity). Plays a central role in mitochondrial calcium homeostasis by mediating mitochondrial calcium extrusion: calcium efflux is essential for mitochondrial function and cell survival, notably in cardiomyocytes (PubMed:40931067). Mitochondrial calcium export is ph-dependent (PubMed:40931067). Regulates rates of glucose-dependent insulin secretion in pancreatic beta-cells during the first phase of insulin secretion: acts by mediating efflux of calcium from mitochondrion, thereby affecting cytoplasmic calcium responses (By similarity). Required for store-operated Ca(2+) entry (SOCE) and Ca(2+) release-activated Ca(2+) (CRAC) channel regulation: sodium transport by SLC8B1 leads to promote calcium-shuttling that modulates mitochondrial redox status, thereby regulating SOCE activity (By similarity). Involved in B-lymphocyte chemotaxis (By similarity). Able to transport Ca(2+) in exchange of either Li(+) or Na(+), explaining how Li(+) catalyzes Ca(2+) exchange (By similarity). In contrast to other members of the family its function is independent of K(+) (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"Ca(2+)(in) + 3 Na(+)(out) = Ca(2+)(out) + 3 Na(+)(in)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:69955"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29101"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29108"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"3 Li(+)(out) + Ca(2+)(in) = 3 Li(+)(in) + Ca(2+)(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:72631"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29108"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:49713"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"}],"value":"Inhibited by the sodium/calcium exchanger inhibitor CGP-37157. Strongly inhibited by zinc"}],"commentType":"ACTIVITY REGULATION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"}],"value":"Interacts with TMEM65; TMEM65 is required fro the mitochondrial sodium/calcium antiporter activity of SLC8B1"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15060069"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20018762"}],"value":"Mitochondrion inner membrane","id":"SL-0168"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15060069"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20018762"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14625281"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15060069"}],"value":"Widely expressed. Present at higher level in pancreas, stomach, skeletal muscle and skin (at protein level). Ubiquitously expressed"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6J4K2"}],"value":"Phosphorylation at Ser-258 by PKA prevents calcium overload"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the Ca(2+):cation antiporter (CaCA) (TC 2.A.19) family. SLC24A subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"40931067"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"The precise mechanism of mitochondrial calcium export is unclear (PubMed:40931067). Based on electron microscopy structures, a publication suggested that SLC8B1 might act as a proton/calcium antiporter instead of a sodium/calcium antiporter (PubMed:40931067). Their arguments are based on the fact that no sodium ions were detected in their structures and sodium-binding sites present in other sodium/calcium antiporters are not conserved in SLC8B1 (PubMed:40931067). Moreover, they showed that the mitochondrial calcium export is pH-dependent without proving the proton transport (PubMed:40931067). Additional evidence are therefore required to confirm the proton/calcium antiporter activity"}],"commentType":"CAUTION"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":26,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":585,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial sodium/calcium exchanger protein","featureId":"PRO_0000045758"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":95,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial matrix","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":96,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":132,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical; Name=1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS1"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS2"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS3"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS4"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS6"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"9PS8"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":133,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":136,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial intermembrane","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start"